.DS_Store
node_modules/
dist/

# While a lock file is a must for a "real" application, the 1,000+ lines of code file and the 1,000+ LOC sized diffs for
# dependency updates detracts from the demo/focus. Let's gitignore it.
#
# I would be ok with a lock file for the true runtime dependencies, but the dev-time dependencies with native binaries,
# like esbuild, bring in a combinatorial explosion of entries, for each combination of OS and CPU:
#
#   - @esbuild/aix-ppc64
#   - @esbuild/android-arm64
#   - @esbuild/android-x64
#   - @esbuild/darwin-arm64
#   - @esbuild/darwin-x64
#   - @esbuild/freebsd-arm64
#   - @esbuild/freebsd-x64
#   - @esbuild/linux-arm64
#   - @esbuild/linux-x64
#   - @esbuild/netbsd-arm64
#   - @esbuild/netbsd-x64
#   - @esbuild/openbsd-arm64
#   - @esbuild/openbsd-x64
#   - @esbuild/openharmony-arm64
#   - @esbuild/sunos-x64
#   - @esbuild/win32-arm64
#   - @esbuild/win32-x64
#
# This noise isn't quite to the level of "security theater", but it's a similar complaint.
#
package-lock.json
